        "original_id": "c7baeaa4-790b-552d-8e5d-b5dfddbd2507",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Carl Ben Eielson\n- Places: Eielson Air Force Base, Fairbanks, Moose Creek, Alaska\n- Organizations: United States Air Force, 168th Wing, 213th Space Warning Squadron\n\nFacts:\n- Carl Benjamin \"Ben\" Eielson was born on July 20, 1897, and died on November 9, 1929.\n- Carl Benjamin \"Ben\" Eielson was an American aviator, bush pilot, and explorer.\n- Eielson Air Force Base in Alaska is named in honor of Carl Benjamin \"Ben\" Eielson.\n- Eielson Air Force Base is a United States Air Force base located about 26 miles southeast of Fairbanks, Alaska, and just southeast of Moose Creek, Alaska.\n- Eielson Air Force Base has the identifiers IATA: EIL, ICAO: PAEI, and FAA LID: EIL.\n- The 213th Space Warning Squadron is a geographically separated unit assigned to the 168th Wing at Eielson Air Force Base.",
